{#
The appearance preview: a mail list and a message, in miniature.

Its own file because it is markup, not logic — the panel around it is already
long — and because keeping it separate makes the one rule about it easy to
state and easy to check: NOTHING HERE IS FETCHED AND NOTHING HERE IS REAL. The
three rows are literal strings from the translation catalogue. There is no
query, no `messages` variable, no route.

What it is not: a second implementation of the thread row. It carries the same
hooks app.css drives the real row through (data-surface, data-account-corner,
data-row-avatar-face, data-row-snippet, row-unread, list-row-y, reading-y), so
the preview and the list are painted by one set of rules. It is a smaller
arrangement of the same parts, not a drawing of them — a drawing would be free
to be wrong.

`@container` on the list: the snippet's two-line clamp is a container query
matching the real list's `@xl`, and this pane is narrow, so the preview shows
the stacked behaviour — which is the one the second line exists for.
#}
{# Sticky within its own column rather than across the top of the panel: the
   controls scroll past it, and it costs the panel width it has instead of
   height it does not.

   `top-0` sticks to the top of the settings pane's scroll port. The opaque
   `bg-surface` that the full-width sticky band needed is gone with it — a side
   column has nothing passing underneath it to read through — and dropping it
   is also the safer contrast answer: this started as `bg-surface/95
   backdrop-blur`, which looked right and measured wrong, the 5% that showed
   through lifting the ground under the sample snippet enough to drop
   --rgb-ink-faint to 4.20:1 in Dark and 4.25:1 in Dusk. The theme guarantees
   that tier ≥4.5:1 ON --rgb-surface (ThemeInkContrastTest holds every theme to
   it), and the bordered block below still paints that surface itself.

   The heading and subtitle sit INSIDE the sticky column, above the coloured
   block, so the thing and its name travel together — left in the main column
   they would have labelled whatever control happened to scroll level with
   them. #}
<section class="sticky top-0"
         aria-label="{{ 'settings.appearance.preview.heading'|trans }}">
    <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink">{{ 'settings.appearance.preview.heading'|trans }}</h2>
    <p class="text-xs text-ink-faint mt-0.5 mb-2">{{ 'settings.appearance.preview.subheading'|trans }}</p>

    {# aria-hidden, and this is deliberate rather than lazy. Every control on
       this page has its own accessible name saying what it does; the preview
       adds no information a screen-reader user can act on, and read out it is
       three invented senders and a paragraph of filler between them and the
       next control. The section keeps its own label so the region is still
       announced and skippable. #}
    <div class="rounded-pane border border-line overflow-hidden" aria-hidden="true">
        <div data-surface="list" class="@container divide-y divide-line">
            {% for row in [
                { unread: true,  seed: 'ada@plmail.test',    tone: 'bg-sky-500/20 text-sky-700 dark:text-sky-300' },
                { unread: false, seed: 'grace@plmail.test',  tone: 'bg-emerald-500/20 text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-300' },
                { unread: false, seed: 'kathleen@plmail.test', tone: 'bg-amber-500/20 text-amber-700 dark:text-amber-300' },
            ] %}
                {# `relative`, because the Strong emphasis bar is an ::before on
                   this element and an absolute child needs a positioned parent
                   — the same reason the real row carries it. #}
                <div class="relative" data-unread="{{ row.unread ? 'true' : 'false' }}" data-preview-row>
                    {% if loop.index == 1 %}
                        <span data-account-corner
                              class="pointer-events-none absolute bottom-0 left-0 h-2.5 w-2.5 bg-sky-500 [clip-path:polygon(0_0,0_100%,100%_100%)]"></span>
                    {% endif %}

                    <div class="flex items-center gap-3 pl-3 pr-3 list-row-y
                                {{ row.unread ? 'row-unread' : 'bg-transparent' }}">
                        <span data-row-avatar-face
                              class="flex items-center justify-center rounded-full w-8 h-8 text-xs font-semibold select-none shrink-0 {{ row.tone }}">
                            {{ ('settings.appearance.preview.sender' ~ loop.index)|trans|first|upper }}
                        </span>

                        <span class="min-w-0 flex-1 flex flex-col">
                            <span class="truncate text-sm {{ row.unread ? 'font-semibold text-ink' : 'font-normal text-ink-muted' }}">
                                {{ ('settings.appearance.preview.sender' ~ loop.index)|trans }}
                            </span>
                            <span class="truncate text-sm mt-0.5 {{ row.unread ? 'font-semibold text-ink' : 'font-normal text-ink-soft' }}">
                                {{ ('settings.appearance.preview.subject' ~ loop.index)|trans }}
                            </span>
                            <span data-row-snippet class="truncate text-sm text-ink-faint mt-0.5">
                                {{ 'settings.appearance.preview.snippet'|trans }}
                            </span>
                        </span>

                        <span class="text-xs text-ink-faint shrink-0">{{ 'now'|date(clock.time) }}</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>

        {# The reading pane half, so the per-surface density controls have
           something to differ against. `mail-sheet` is the real utility: the
           reading pane switches to the theme's light sheet in every theme, and
           a preview that kept the app's surface would show the setting against
           the wrong background. #}
        <div data-surface="reading" class="mail-sheet border-t border-line px-3">
            <div class="reading-y">
                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                    <span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-sky-500/20 text-sky-700 text-[10px] font-semibold flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">
                        {{ 'settings.appearance.preview.sender1'|trans|first|upper }}
                    </span>
                    <span class="text-xs font-semibold text-ink truncate">{{ 'settings.appearance.preview.sender1'|trans }}</span>
                </div>
                <p class="text-xs text-ink-soft mt-1.5 leading-relaxed">{{ 'settings.appearance.preview.body'|trans }}</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
